-- Node: ami-resus (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":3,"title":"Resuscitation — The 11 As","body":"[The 11 As Checklist](#/info/ami-11as)\n\n**Start immediately while awaiting definitive treatment:**\n\n1. **Aggressive fluids** — LR boluses, blood products PRN\n2. **Address metabolic derangements** — correct acidosis, K+, Mg2+\n3. **Antibiotics** — [Pip-tazo 4.5g IV q6h](#/drug/piperacillin-tazobactam/ami)\n4. **Anticoagulation** — [Heparin](#/drug/ufh/ami) 100 U/kg bolus → 18 U/kg/hr (use local protocol for maximum and monitoring adjustments)\n5. **Analgesia** — IV opioids (do NOT withhold)\n6. **Avoid vasopressors** — worsen ischemia\n7. **Alleviate distension** — NG tube\n8. **Avoid hyperoxia** — target SpO2 96-99%\n9. **Advance directives** — discuss GOC early\n10. **Abdominal compartment syndrome** — monitor bladder pressures\n11. **All the help** — Vascular, General Surgery, IR, ICU","citation":[2,4,5],"next":"ami-anticoag","summary":"The 11 As: Aggressive fluids, Antibiotics, Anticoagulation, Analgesia, Avoid vasopressors, consults."}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'ami-resus' AND tree_id = 'mesenteric-ischemia';

-- Node: ami-anticoag (2 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":3,"title":"Anticoagulation — Start Early","body":"**Unfractionated Heparin (preferred):**\n\n• **Bolus:** [Heparin](#/drug/ufh/ami) **100 U/kg IV** when AMI is suspected (use local protocol for maximum and adjustments)\n• **Infusion:** 18 U/kg/hr\n• **Goal aPTT:** 40-60 seconds\n\n**Why heparin:**\n• Can be rapidly reversed with protamine if surgery needed\n• Early anticoagulation improves survival\n• Prevents clot propagation\n\n🛑 **Do NOT delay anticoagulation waiting for surgery**\n\nStart immediately; it can be reversed if OR needed urgently.","citation":[2,4],"next":"ami-abx","summary":"Heparin 100 U/kg bolus → 18 U/kg/hr, goal aPTT 40-60. Start immediately — can reverse with protamine if needed."}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'ami-anticoag' AND tree_id = 'mesenteric-ischemia';

-- Node: rosc-start (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":1,"title":"ROSC Confirmed — Immediate Priorities","body":"[Post-ROSC Steps Summary](#/info/rosc-steps-summary)\n\nROSC confirmed. Immediate priorities:\n\n**Airway & Ventilation:**\n• Secure airway if not already — intubate if GCS ≤8\n• Waveform capnography to confirm ETT placement\n• Target ETCO₂ 35-45 mmHg — guides ventilation\n\n**Immediate Workup:**\n• **12-lead ECG** — STEMI identification is the #1 priority\n• Avoid hypoxemia (SpO₂ <90%) and hypotension (MAP <65)\n• Arterial line for continuous BP monitoring\n• Labs: ABG, lactate, troponin, BMP, CBC, coags\n• Portable CXR (ETT position, pulmonary edema)","citation":[1,2,5],"next":"rosc-stemi","summary":"Secure airway, 12-lead ECG immediately, target ETCO2 35-45, arterial line, labs/CXR","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'rosc-start' AND tree_id = 'post-rosc';

-- Node: rosc-hemo (2 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":2,"title":"Hemodynamic Targets","body":"**Hemodynamic and gas-exchange targets:**\n• **MAP ≥65 mmHg** — avoid hypotension; use fluids and vasopressor/inotrope support as clinically indicated\n• **SpO₂ 90-98%** or **PaO₂ 60-105 mmHg** — avoid hypoxemia and severe hyperoxemia (PaO₂ >250 mmHg has been associated with worse outcomes)\n• **PaCO₂ 35-45 mmHg** — avoid hypocapnia (cerebral vasoconstriction)\n• **ETCO₂ 35-45 mmHg** — use as a ventilation trend, confirmed with blood gas when needed\n\nOnce a reliable oxygenation measurement is available, titrate FiO₂ to the target range. Use 100% oxygen until SpO₂ or PaO₂ can be measured reliably.","citation":[1,2,5,6],"next":"rosc-pressors","summary":"MAP >=65, SpO2 90-98% or PaO2 60-105, PaCO2 35-45 — titrate FiO2 down once reliable oxygenation is measured","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'rosc-hemo' AND tree_id = 'post-rosc';

-- Node: rosc-pressors (3 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":2,"title":"Vasopressor Support","body":"**Vasopressor and inotrope support:**\n\n**AHA 2025:** There is insufficient evidence to recommend one specific vasopressor for undifferentiated post-ROSC hypotension. Choose support based on the shock phenotype, bedside echo, rhythm, and perfusion.\n\n• For vasodilatory shock, [Norepinephrine](#/drug/norepinephrine/post cardiac arrest) is a reasonable commonly used option: 0.1-0.5 mcg/kg/min\n• Refractory vasodilatory shock: consider [Vasopressin](#/drug/vasopressin/post cardiac arrest) 0.04 units/min\n• If cardiac dysfunction: [Dobutamine](#/drug/dobutamine/cardiogenic shock) 2-20 mcg/kg/min or [Milrinone](#/drug/milrinone/cardiogenic shock) may be appropriate with ICU/cardiology guidance\n• Echo to assess LV function — post-arrest myocardial stunning is common and may recover over 24-72h\n\nAvoid reflexive selection of any single agent. Reassess perfusion, lactate, rhythm, and ventricular function after each intervention.","citation":[1,5,6,15],"next":"rosc-ttm-check","summary":"No single post-ROSC vasopressor is preferred by AHA; tailor fluids, vasopressor, and inotrope support to shock phenotype"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'rosc-pressors' AND tree_id = 'post-rosc';

-- Node: rosc-ttm-coma (2 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":3,"title":"Comatose — Prevent Fever Aggressively","body":"**Patient not following commands after ROSC: initiate deliberate temperature control.**\n\n**TTM2 Trial (2021):** 33°C vs 37.5°C showed no difference in mortality or neurological outcome.\n\n**AHA 2025:**\n• Maintain a controlled temperature between **32°C and 37.5°C**\n• Maintain temperature control for **at least 36 hours**\n• If using a normothermia strategy, actively prevent fever and keep temperature below 37.5°C\n• Routine rapid infusion of cold IV fluid for prehospital cooling is not recommended\n\n**Anti-shivering protocol:**\n• [Magnesium Sulfate](#/drug/magnesium-sulfate/ttm) 4g IV (raises shivering threshold)\n• Sedation: propofol or midazolam infusion\n• [Meperidine](#/drug/meperidine/shivering) 25-50mg IV (centrally acting)\n• Neuromuscular blockade if refractory\n\n**Monitor:** Core temperature continuously (esophageal or bladder probe). Avoid uncontrolled fever and unintended overcooling.","citation":[2,3,4,10],"next":"rosc-neuro","summary":"TTM2: no benefit of routine 33C cooling — control temperature at 32-37.5C for at least 36h and prevent fever","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'rosc-ttm-coma' AND tree_id = 'post-rosc';

-- Node: rosc-ttm-awake (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":3,"title":"Following Commands — Standard Care","body":"Following commands = good neurological sign.\n\n**Standard care:**\n• Monitor temperature and treat clinically significant fever per ICU protocol\n• No post-arrest temperature-control pathway is required solely because the patient is awake and following commands\n• Continue hemodynamic optimization\n• Workup for arrest cause (echo, labs, serial ECGs)\n• Neurology consult if any concern for seizure activity","citation":[2,6],"next":"rosc-neuro","summary":"Awake post-ROSC — standard care, treat fever, echo for arrest cause, neuro consult if seizure concern","skippable":true}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'rosc-ttm-awake' AND tree_id = 'post-rosc';

-- Node: rosc-neuro (3 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":4,"title":"Neuroprognostication — Wait 72h Minimum","body":"**⚠️ Do NOT make a prognostic impression before at least 72 hours from ROSC or achievement of normothermia, and only after sedation, hypothermia, neuromuscular blockade, and other confounders have cleared.**\n\nPremature withdrawal of care can cause an avoidable death.\n\n**Multimodal approach:**\n• **Clinical exam:** interpret brainstem reflexes and motor response in context, after confounders clear\n• **EEG:** background, seizures, and malignant patterns\n• **SSEP:** bilaterally absent N20 cortical responses can provide highly specific evidence when technically valid\n• **CT/MRI:** diffuse anoxic injury pattern\n• **NSE and neurofilament light (NfL):** may support prognostication when available and interpreted with the rest of the assessment; do not use a single biomarker threshold alone\n\n**No single test is sufficient.** Require multimodal, concordant evidence and communicate uncertainty before any withdrawal discussion.","citation":[6,8,9,12,15],"next":"rosc-seizure","summary":"Delay prognostic impressions until >=72h from ROSC or normothermia and after confounders clear; use multimodal evidence","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'rosc-neuro' AND tree_id = 'post-rosc';

-- Node: rosc-seizure (2 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":4,"title":"Post-Arrest Seizures","body":"**Post-arrest seizures** occur in 20-30% of comatose survivors.\n\n• Obtain continuous or repeated EEG in patients who do not follow commands and when seizures are suspected\n• Clinical seizures may be subtle (eye twitching, nystagmus) or masked by paralysis\n• **Do not give routine antiseizure prophylaxis** when there is no seizure or ictal-interictal EEG pattern\n• Treatment when indicated: [Levetiracetam](#/drug/levetiracetam/status epilepticus) 60 mg/kg IV (max 4500mg) — first-line\n• Refractory: valproate, phenobarbital, midazolam/propofol infusion\n• **Myoclonus ≠ seizure:** do not suppress myoclonus without an EEG correlate solely to improve outcome; Lance-Adams syndrome may have a better prognosis than early post-hypoxic status epilepticus","citation":[5,6,8,15],"next":"rosc-icu-targets","summary":"20-30% have post-arrest seizures — continuous EEG, levetiracetam first-line, myoclonus is not always seizure","safetyLevel":"warning"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'rosc-seizure' AND tree_id = 'post-rosc';

